# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE BUILD CONTRACT — do not remove this file.
#
# Found 2026-07-29 by cloning the repo cold and running the battery: the clone
# checked out CRLF (Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true) and everything
# downstream broke.
#
#   * make-probe-build.js locates the game IIFE by the exact string
#     "\n})();\n</script>". Under CRLF that anchor does not exist, so it exits
#     "IIFE close not found" -> validate.js fails -> smoke, the fingerprint and
#     the deploy gate all fail. A fresh clone could not verify anything.
#   * celestial-frontier.html grew 26,717 bytes (1,935,361 -> 1,962,078) purely
#     in carriage returns. The whole project is built around one small file on
#     one link; a 1.4% payload tax for nothing is not acceptable.
#   * main.js is gitignored and regenerated from the html by extract.js, so a
#     CRLF html silently produces a CRLF main.js and every byte-exact string
#     anchor in the tooling becomes unreliable.
#
# The tool was also made line-ending tolerant, so this is belt and braces — but
# the artifact itself must stay LF, because it is what ships.

* text=auto eol=lf

# binaries must never be touched
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
